WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:35.048 --> 00:00:36.590
That was one thing
that really struck

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:41.060
me was the speed at which
the streets became vacant.

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:43.280
Times Square, Abbey
Road, you know,

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.000
these are areas that are
always teeming with people.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.110
The Temple Bar area in Dublin.

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:53.198
There's always folks there,
day and night, always.

00:00:53.198 --> 00:00:55.490
It's significant, and I've
never seen anything like it,

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:58.650
having this global
network of cameras.

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:01.100
Especially after 9/11,
everywhere in New York

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:02.930
was really quiet.

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:06.270
And it was similar, but
it wasn't to this extent.

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:07.790
And certainly
globally, it wasn't

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:10.070
anything like what
we're experiencing now.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:13.560
Our purpose is better lives
through visual information.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:17.660
So what better than giving this
visual information to people

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:21.350
to help them in a time like
this explore the planet,

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:24.560
feel comfort in the fact that
the world is still out there,

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.360
we're all going to
get back out there.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:27.380
You can still go there.

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:31.700
You can still go sit on a beach
virtually and experience things

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:35.840
that you will hopefully be
able to experience very soon

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:37.610
again in real life.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:04.820
This camera is allowing
us to appreciate

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:09.160
the beauty of the city, but of
course a city without citizen,

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:10.650
it is not a really city.

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:13.880
It's like just a postcard,
something unbelievable,

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:19.000
something amazing, but
something also unreal, no?

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:22.750
Because citizens are
the soul of the city.

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:23.870
And we are a hotel.

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:29.500
So hotel cannot exist without
tourists, especially Venice,

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:33.960
because 90 per cent of the
tourists are also international

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:34.980
tourists.

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:41.820
There is a lot of
uncertainty in town about how

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:44.190
we are supposed to reopen.

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:48.600
Because I think it's quite
difficult to welcome guests

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:54.400
with masks, with temperature
control, and with this disease,

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:54.900
no?

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:17.210
So since lockdown came into
force on the 23rd of March

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:21.110
we've had about 20 times as many
visitors to our webcam's page

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:24.260
that we would expect at
this time of the year.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.180
While we already
know that people

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:29.390
feel happier and healthier when
they're connected with nature,

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:31.730
but at a time like this,
when we're more isolated

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:33.740
from the people that
we're closest to,

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:36.350
spending that time
connecting with wildlife

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:38.420
through the screen
can actually help

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:41.110
to make you feel a lot
better in yourself.

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:44.328
And they're like the most
addictive soap operas, really.

00:03:44.328 --> 00:03:45.620
You get to know the characters.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.930
You get to know the individual
badgers, the barn owls,

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:50.870
the puffins... and you just want
to keep going back and getting

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:52.250
to know them even better.

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:55.040
So it can really help soothe
our souls at the moment.

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:01.910
I think the extraordinary thing
that this pandemic has shown

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:04.730
is what once again,
we're all in it together.

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:08.280
This is a global crisis,
as indeed is the climate

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:09.810
and ecological crisis.

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:12.800
Nearly everyone...
we've changed our lives.

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:15.620
You have people who
are frontline workers

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:18.560
in your family, or the people
who are obviously suffering.

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:20.240
But also there are
changes to the lives

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:21.667
which may be for the better.

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:23.750
So for example, you might
actually spend more time

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:25.070
with your family.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:28.460
You might spend a little
less time commuting.

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:32.240
And indeed, you might
connect more to nature

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:33.060
on your doorstep.

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:37.580
Now all of that qualities,
emotions, and experiences,

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:40.985
which I think somehow we'll need
to capture when we do emerge.

00:04:56.385 --> 00:04:59.600
I've kind of akinned
it to a Sunday morning.

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:02.430
I've been working
shifts for 50-odd years,

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:06.200
and Sunday morning's always
that kind of easy, easy time

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:09.540
you could just take
stock and then catch up

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:10.845
a bit of a backlog of things.

00:05:10.845 --> 00:05:12.470
Because there's not
much else going on.

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:15.058
And that's what we're seeing
most days at the moment.

00:05:15.058 --> 00:05:16.600
Because there's less
traffic as well,

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:17.975
the speeds have
gone up slightly.

00:05:17.975 --> 00:05:19.970
Because normally
in central London,

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:22.740
you'd maybe get 5, 10 miles
an hour if you're lucky.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:27.185
The accidents we're getting
are more serious kind

00:05:27.185 --> 00:05:28.940
of damage-wise.

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:32.270
We've got a balcony up on
the seventh floor here.

00:05:32.270 --> 00:05:34.280
You go up there for
a cup of coffee,

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:36.600
and you can hear
the birds tweeting,

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:39.230
you can hear the odd
rumble of the odd train.

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:40.220
But that's it.

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:42.965
And that is very peculiar.

00:05:42.965 --> 00:05:43.590
This is London.

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:44.673
It shouldn't be like this.

00:05:44.673 --> 00:05:47.900
It should be hustle,
bustle, horns, sirens,

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:50.237
everything going off,
trains rumbling past.

00:05:50.237 --> 00:05:51.320
A bit un-nerving in a way.

00:05:58.277 --> 00:06:02.320
Especially during this crisis,
lots of people from their home

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:05.530
are curious what's going
on in the next city,

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:07.730
or on the opposite
side of the world.

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:11.110
People use it as
a virtual window.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:19.630
In construction sites saves
the person of the office travel

00:06:19.630 --> 00:06:24.430
time, and that will not change
after the crisis is over.

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:27.400
Because they got
accustomed to the fact

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:30.700
that they can watch
remotely, and so no longer

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:33.610
need to be in traffic
for one or two hours.

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:36.520
And we have seen an
increase of requests

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:42.250
for, once this crisis is over,
the regulations will change.

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:45.010
And of course, a theatre
or cinema needs to take

00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:46.520
precautions.

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:51.000
One of the precautions now
is instal thermal cameras.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:55.780
And a thermal camera is because
our body has a temperature, 37

00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:57.640
degrees, or 36.5.

00:06:57.640 --> 00:07:01.270
You will see the difference
between a sick person

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:02.410
and a not sick person.

00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:06.880
We get hundreds of
people watching.

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:09.670
Because they like to watch the
streets, people walking by.

00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:12.220
And I guess they look
like they're people

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:14.200
watching, but from their home.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.690
And unfortunately,
obviously, the bars and stuff

00:07:16.690 --> 00:07:17.980
are closed in Thailand now.

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:20.530
So we don't really get that
many views through it now.

00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:22.720
Because there's nothing
for people to watch.

00:07:25.350 --> 00:07:27.560
But the one that's
getting the most attention

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:31.910
now is called Samui
Yacht Club, and it's

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:33.660
like a view of the sea.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:35.990
Some people write and say
they find it very relaxing.

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:37.370
They put it on in
the background,

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:40.690
and they just like to hear
the sea noise and stuff.

